4-5"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"TE Kevin Bigelow complained against multiple actions of North Florida Presbytery related to the dissolution of his call as Assistant Pastor of Christ Church East (where he was also serving as planting pastor at Christ Church Beaches). The SJC sustained the complaint in part (22-0-0), finding that Presbytery erred in…"}},{"id":"bco:22-4--case:cases/ga52_2025__2024-01.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga52_2025__2024-01.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Moehn v. Westminster Presbytery","year":2025,"disposition":"sustained","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga52_2025__2024-01.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga52_2025__2024-01.md","evidence_basis":"structured_case_metadata","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:22-4--case:cases/ga52_2025__2024-01.md:occ-93c6a0d5ddfa","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga52_2025__2024-01.html","repository_path":"cases/ga52_2025__2024-01.md","locator":{},"excerpt":"","sources":["cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga52_2025__2024-01.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["biblical divorce","desertion","WCF 24.6","1 Corinthians 7","BCO 31-2 investigation","marriage dissolution","professing believer","willful desertion","divorce grounds"],"case_numbers":["2024-1"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"TE Andy Moehn complained that Westminster Presbytery erred in its BCO 31-2 investigation of his wife Kacey Moehn regarding alleged desertion and in declaring the question of biblical divorce grounds moot. The SJC sustained the complaint 21-1-0, finding that Presbytery used an extra-confessional interpretation of WCF…"}},{"id":"bco:22-4--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"David Kniseley et al. v. Rocky Mountain Presbytery","year":2009,"disposition":"denied","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:22-4--case:cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md:occ-a125f88e47b4","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.html","repository_path":"cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":262},"excerpt":"2. BCO 22-4 shall read: The relationship of the Associate Pastor to the church is determined by the congregation. The relationship of the Assistant Pastor to the church is determined by the Session. The dissolution of the relationship of both is governed by…","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga37_2009__2007-13.md"}],"metadata":{"topics":["minister title","non-ordained staff","women","constitutional interpretation","presbytery judgment"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2007-13"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"On complaint from TE David Kniseley and others, the SJC reviewed Rocky Mountain Presbytery's refusal to forbid a mission church from giving an unordained female staff member the title 'Minister of Church Life.' The SJC denied the complaint. It held the BCO uses 'minister' synonymously with pastor and teaching elder, but is silent on general use for non-ordained staff; a lower court may exercise discretion subject to BCO 40-2(3)'s WESP review. The decision addressed only the constitutional issue, not the title's wisdom or propriety; four commissioners dissented."}},{"id":"bco:22-4--overture:ga33_2005:7","record_id":"overture:ga33_2005:7","type":"Overture","title":"Amend BCO 21-5, 6, 7, 8, 10 and 22-4 Regarding Assistant Pastors","year":2005,"disposition":"Answered in the negative","authority_weight":"low-but-important","url":"https: